WEBVTT

00:00:05.306 --> 00:00:11.226
Welcome to today's deep dive. I mean imagine you build this pristine like five-star luxury car

00:00:11.546 --> 00:00:17.986
But when you go to sell it the dealership insists on paying you the price of a rusted used bicycle

00:00:18.506 --> 00:00:22.426
That is exactly what is happening to Puerto Rico's health care system right now

00:00:22.586 --> 00:00:28.026
Yeah, it really is a massive contradiction when you dig into the CMS data consoles and enrollment research

00:00:28.066 --> 00:00:34.266
You see this glaring anomaly. I mean Puerto Rico has the highest medicare advantage penetration in the entire US

00:00:34.266 --> 00:00:39.506
Right over 96% exactly 96.2% and they are getting top tier clinical quality yet

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:44.426
They receive the absolute lowest federal health care funding in the nation and for you listening

00:00:44.426 --> 00:00:46.786
This isn't just some you know boring policy quirk

00:00:46.906 --> 00:00:53.506
This is a masterclass in how massive gaps in federal funding actually force a local market to innovate just to survive

00:00:53.506 --> 00:00:59.306
So true and to understand why practically everyone chooses medicare advantage or MA over traditional medicare

00:00:59.346 --> 00:01:01.586
We really have to look at what they aren't getting

00:01:01.586 --> 00:01:05.866
Let's compare say Elena in Puerto Rico to Rosa in Florida, okay?

00:01:05.866 --> 00:01:11.346
So both are paying the exact same medicare payroll taxes their whole lives, right?

00:01:11.346 --> 00:01:16.506
But Rosa in Florida has access to this whole federal safety net. She gets

00:01:17.066 --> 00:01:19.706
supplemental security income medicare savings programs

00:01:20.666 --> 00:01:25.506
Part D extra help for prescriptions and long-term care Medicaid and Elena in Puerto Rico

00:01:25.506 --> 00:01:28.706
She gets none of that right none of it. She is completely excluded

00:01:28.706 --> 00:01:35.626
So that creates a federal support gap of roughly three thousand four hundred dollars a month Wow three fee four hundred dollars every single month

00:01:35.626 --> 00:01:40.746
That is huge it is and it makes standard traditional medicare basically useless for Elena

00:01:40.866 --> 00:01:45.986
If she wanted full coverage like standard medicare plus a medigap policy and a drug plan

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:52.306
She'd be paying around four hundred fifty dollars a month out of pocket which on a fixed income in Puerto Rico is literally impossible

00:01:52.346 --> 00:01:56.746
So she chooses medicare advantage because it steps in and offers a zero dollar premium

00:01:56.746 --> 00:02:03.146
Yeah, and they bundle in vital supplemental benefits to stuff traditional medicare ignores like dental vision and transportation

00:02:03.146 --> 00:02:05.346
It's kind of like traditional medicare is a smartphone

00:02:05.426 --> 00:02:09.266
But for someone in Puerto Rico the battery in the screen are sold separately

00:02:09.266 --> 00:02:15.466
Yeah, so MA plans essentially manufacture their own batteries and give away a fully working phone for free

00:02:15.826 --> 00:02:17.826
Just to patch those holes in the safety net

00:02:17.826 --> 00:02:20.746
That's a perfect way to put it but here is where it gets wild

00:02:21.026 --> 00:02:26.986
You would assume given they rely entirely on MA with such limited funds that the care would be bare bones

00:02:27.306 --> 00:02:31.666
But it's actually the exact opposite wait really how good are we talking well?

00:02:32.706 --> 00:02:37.986
99.1% of Puerto Rican MA patients are enrolled in plans rated 4.5 stars or higher by CMS

00:02:38.266 --> 00:02:43.266
The three largest five-star MA contracts in the entire US are in Puerto Rico

00:02:43.266 --> 00:02:46.746
Okay, hold on. I have to jump in here if they are delivering five-star care

00:02:47.346 --> 00:02:50.706
Shouldn't the federal government be rewarding that I mean Puerto Rico's benchmark is only

00:02:51.546 --> 00:02:55.506
$778 a month right well the US average is over $1300

00:02:55.506 --> 00:02:58.026
Yeah, $1313 to be exact

00:02:58.026 --> 00:03:03.066
It makes no sense until you look at the historical roots from the 1930s through the 1980s

00:03:03.066 --> 00:03:05.466
Puerto Rico had a government-run healthcare model

00:03:05.466 --> 00:03:08.586
So doctors weren't really billing medicare like they did on the mainland

00:03:09.106 --> 00:03:13.826
Exactly, they didn't do standard fee-for-service billing so that artificially and permanently

00:03:13.906 --> 00:03:17.306
Depressed the historical data used to calculate today's MA rates

00:03:17.346 --> 00:03:20.586
So CMS is financially starving a five-star market today

00:03:20.706 --> 00:03:25.666
Just because their grandfathers didn't file mainland style paperwork 50 years ago sadly. Yes

00:03:25.666 --> 00:03:29.786
And because 96.2% of seniors are in MA now

00:03:30.346 --> 00:03:37.546
Traditional fee-for-service basically doesn't exist there. So the government keeps calculating the funding based on a statistically flawed

00:03:38.106 --> 00:03:43.506
Tiny sliver of patients. It's a mathematical death spiral. That is completely wild

00:03:43.506 --> 00:03:48.266
How do we even fix a broken formula like that? Well, the message to the federal government is simple

00:03:48.266 --> 00:03:52.026
You have the administrative authority to fix this right now. You don't need Congress

00:03:52.306 --> 00:03:58.106
Just use the neighboring US Virgin Islands fee-for-service rates as a proxy and adjust the formula tomorrow, right?

00:03:58.106 --> 00:04:02.466
So to the local government and the patients you just have to keep shouting from the rooftops

00:04:02.986 --> 00:04:09.466
Because out of sheer necessity you have built a world-class system and to the general public, you know

00:04:10.026 --> 00:04:15.986
This is about the fundamental promise of American health care equity when we fund excellence equitably

00:04:16.426 --> 00:04:19.946
Every single citizen thrives no matter where they live. Absolutely

00:04:20.386 --> 00:04:22.746
Think about that luxury car in a bicycle budget

00:04:22.746 --> 00:04:29.506
Yeah, if a chronically underfunded island can build the nation's most cost effective five-star health care model against all odds

00:04:30.146 --> 00:04:35.066
Imagine what health care innovations they could teach the rest of the country if they were just given a level playing field

